cartridge "SPACE CHASE/CZES KOSNIOWSKI/1983"

' SPACE CHASE - ColecoVision version of the Oric game by Czes Kosniowski
' ("Games to Play on Your Oric-1", Shiva, 1983, game 21).
' Adapted by Amy & Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this
' file, ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): your ship, short of fuel, flies on full thrust
' through a field that scrolls down; the joystick steers it left and right.
' Fly into the energy sources (the book's asterisks, +250) and avoid the
' cosmic debris: each crash costs one of the crashes you chose to allow
' (1-9). After any hit there is one chance in two of a new energy source.
'
' CONTROLS: joystick only. Title: up/down choose, left/right change the
' starting level and the number of ships, a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - Smooth vertical scroll (1 pixel steps) instead of the Oric's line
'   scroll; the ship is a sprite that moves 2 pixels a frame.
' - The fuel shortage of the book's story is a real gauge: it drains, an
'   energy source refills a third of it, an empty tank costs a ship.
' - Levels: ten energy sources clear a level (the book went on until the
'   last crash); later levels scroll faster with more debris.
' - "Number of crashes allowed" is the SHIPS choice of the title (1-9,
'   default 5), shown as ship icons.
' - A crash removes the debris and gives 2 seconds of safety (the ship
'   blinks at 1.9 Hz); the book's red / yellow / green paper flashes are
'   kept as short backdrop flashes.
' - Two kinds of debris (grey rock, red-hot fragment) and two kinds of
'   stars (scenery only); colour, music and sound effects are new.

